# Web app (Vite). Copy to web/.env (or .env.local) — or set in your host's
# build settings. Vite inlines VITE_* vars at BUILD time, so set these before
# `npm run build -w web`; a built bundle is pinned to whatever they were.

# ── The one switch: which chain is this build for? ────────────────────────────
# testnet | mainnet. Everything chain-shaped is derived from this — algod URL,
# block explorer, USDC asset id, CAIP-2 network id, and the network label in the
# UI — so the app can't end up half on one chain and half on the other.
#
# Must match the backend's ALGORAND_NETWORK. Mismatch and every payment fails
# verification: the client signs for one chain, the facilitator checks another.
VITE_ALGORAND_NETWORK=testnet

# Base URL of the Tendril registry the web app talks to.
# Local dev:
VITE_REGISTRY_URL=http://localhost:4000
# Production example (must be HTTPS if the site is served over HTTPS):
# VITE_REGISTRY_URL=https://api.your-tendril-domain.com

# ── Optional per-value overrides ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only for a private algod or a self-hosted explorer. Leave both unset and they
# follow VITE_ALGORAND_NETWORK. Set one and it stops following — point it at the
# same network you set above.
#
# Algod endpoint the wallet uses to build + sign payments.
# VITE_ALGOD_URL=https://testnet-api.algonode.cloud
#
# Block explorer the dashboard links txns/accounts to (no trailing slash).
# VITE_EXPLORER_URL=https://lora.algokit.io/testnet

# Magic publishable key (pk_live_… / pk_test_…) from https://dashboard.magic.link.
# Enables social sign-in in the connect modal (Google + email OTP). Magic custodies
# an Algorand account for the user, so someone with no wallet can rent compute.
# Publishable by design — it is meant to ship in the bundle.
#
# In Magic Dashboard: enable Email OTP + Google under Social Login, add your site
# origin to allowed origins, and set OAuth redirect to {origin}/callback.
# Create the Magic app as an Algorand project (not Ethereum-only). rpcUrl stays
# empty in code — Magic docs require it. If you see "blockchain no longer
# supported", your API key is from a non-Algorand Magic app or Magic removed
# Algorand for new projects; create a fresh Algorand-enabled app in the dashboard.
#
# LEAVE UNSET and the connect button behaves exactly as before: Pera / Lute /
# Defly only, no social branch. Nothing else in the app depends on it.
# VITE_MAGIC_API_KEY=pk_live_XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
